AI-Native Ecosystem: Orchestration with Purpose (NTT DATA, 2026)

Summary

This whitepaper explores how Generative AI transforms enterprise applications into AI-native ecosystems centered on semantics, orchestration, governance, and trust. It introduces concepts such as semantic modernization, AI orchestration, trust assurance, and Cognitive Confidence Levels (CCLs) for evaluating AI-assisted decision processes.

Why it matters

Although primarily focused on AI-native application architectures, the paper highlights several concepts highly relevant to Industrial Decision Intelligence:

AI Orchestration and human-AI collaboration
Semantic architectures and explainability
Decision traceability and governance
Trust assurance for AI-generated recommendations
The shift from application-centric to intelligence-centric enterprise architectures

Relation to virtauto

The paper aligns with virtauto's vision of an Enterprise Decision Layer by emphasizing governance, traceability, and orchestration. While the paper focuses on AI-native applications, virtauto extends this perspective by placing Decision Intelligence and Organizational Agency at the center of enterprise architecture.

